    "explanation": "Both sides agree on the material facts, and the record confirms them, so this case is decided on the waiting clock. ARRIVAL: EV-GPS-03202 shows the driver holding position inside the 50 m STANDARD arrival radius at Blk 108 Yishun Ring Rd on 11 consecutive fixes from 12:21:22, the same timestamp as the 'I'm Here' event in EV-TRIP-03202. POL-NS-02 is satisfied and POL-NS-01 limbs (a) and (b) hold; the marker was not false, because the fix at the marker's own timestamp is the first in-geofence fix, so POL-NS-05 does not fire and no false-arrival referral is issued. The driver's arguments on this point are accepted, as is the rider's concession that the driver did arrive. WAITING PERIOD: the fee fails at POL-NS-01 limb (c). The driver's whole in-geofence time is a single continuous run of 95 seconds, from 12:21:22 to 12:22:57, against the 180-second free waiting period in force for this trip (trip_record.platform_policy.free_wait_sec) - a shortfall of 85 seconds. There is no second in-geofence interval, and the only advisory covering this pickup, EV-ADVIS-03202-01, is MISSING at weight 0.0, so POL-NS-06(i) accumulation is unavailable; that absent artifact carries no deciding fact and does not lower confidence. LIMB (d): the driver terminated at 12:23:01 under RIDER_NO_SHOW, before the required dwell had elapsed, so limb (d) is not satisfied either - it requires the cancellation to fall at or after the moment the dwell elapsed. The driver's submission that the reason code is truthful is rejected on that timing; the cancellation was premature. RIDER'S CONDUCT: the driver's statement that the rider was 'nowhere near my car' is not supported by the record - the rider's track in EV-GPS-03202 carries 41 fixes, all within 18.05 m of the pin, and EV-CHAT-03202 shows the rider at 12:22:22 saying she was at the lobby, the driver replying at 12:22:37, and the driver posting his car's position at 12:22:57, four seconds before cancelling. POL-NS-04 does not exonerate the rider because the driver replied within 120 seconds, and it does not need to: POL-NS-06 refunds the fee whether or not the rider was present or responsive. WHAT IS PAYABLE: POL-NS-06 requires the cancellation fee to be refunded in full. EV-FARE-03202 shows the 4.50 SGD cancellation fee charged (total_charged 4.50, payment_status CHARGED, refund_issued_sgd 0.00), so the whole of that 4.50 SGD is returned to the rider and the charge does not stand. No driver compensation is payable: POL-NS-06 awards none where the dwell falls short, and the POL-NS-07 anti-farming check does not trip in any case (driver_profile.no_show_terminations_30d 1 against completed_trips_30d 62, a rate of 1.6 percent, so neither limb of that check is met). ESCALATION: no POL-NS-09 trigger fires - the same-pair dispute counts are 0 and 0, rider_profile.no_show_disputes_30d is 1, and the deciding facts rest on EV-GPS-03202 and EV-TRIP-03202, both COMPLETE at weight 1.0, so the POL-GEN-02(2) cap is 1.0, above the 0.70 floor; confidence is 0.95. EXECUTION AND REFERRALS: the monetary effect of 4.50 SGD is below the 8.00 SGD execution threshold in POL-GEN-05, so it executes on issue. No referral is issued, because no clause produces one on these facts: the POL-NS-05(ii) false-arrival record is not triggered, and POL-NS-01's driver-education referral attaches to a mis-selected reason code, whereas RIDER_NO_SHOW is one of the codes limb (d) recognises. For the record only: the driver cancelled 99 seconds after arriving under a no-show code, which the platform may wish to note as a pattern, but no clause mandates a referral for it."
